    "text": "Which is bigger: three quarters or one half? Let’s build the amounts and find out.",
    "chapter": "Which is bigger?",
    "equation": [
      [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "?",
      [
        1,
        2
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
        "n": 3,
        "d": 4,
        "label": "Three quarters",
        "colour": "teal"
      },
      {
        "n": 1,
        "d": 2,
        "label": "One half",
        "colour": "gold"
      }
    ],
    "note": "Always compare the same-sized whole.",
    "line": null,
    "area": null,
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 1,
    "start": 4.307800453514739,
    "end": 9.747845804988662,
    "samples": 119953,
    "audio_sha256": "593affa768ccda2077fca7baedf1fb3d255797a0c237997a188777865e74ce00",
    "text": "A fraction starts with equal parts. Here, one whole is divided into four equal pieces.",
    "chapter": "Equal parts make fractions",
    "equation": [
      [
        1,
        4
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [],
    "note": "Each piece is one quarter.",
    "line": null,
    "area": [
      1,
      4
    ],
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 2,
    "start": 9.747845804988662,
    "end": 17.246349206349205,
    "samples": 165342,
    "audio_sha256": "5e27a60b644dfe22aa4f5393c422d006303e42765447998ede20c02ede987802",
    "text": "Shade three pieces. The numerator, three, counts the shaded parts. The denominator, four, counts the equal parts in the whole.",
    "chapter": "Read the fraction",
    "equation": [
      [
        3,
        4
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [],
    "note": "Numerator: parts chosen. Denominator: equal parts in one whole.",
    "line": null,
    "area": [
      3,
      4
    ],
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 3,
    "start": 17.246349206349205,
    "end": 23.556643990929704,
    "samples": 139142,
    "audio_sha256": "61f17402e0db64aeb1286a4ee5df5fea480b18519f5145d00b7c404fc90a2bce",
    "text": "A strip shows the same amount. Three of four equal lengths are shaded. The picture changes, but the value stays the same.",
    "chapter": "Different model, same value",
    "equation": [
      [
        3,
        4
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
        "n": 3,
        "d": 4,
        "label": "Three equal quarter-lengths",
        "colour": "teal"
      }
    ],
    "note": "Area models and strips show the same fraction.",
    "line": null,
    "area": null,
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 4,
    "start": 23.556643990929704,
    "end": 30.636371882086166,
    "samples": 156108,
    "audio_sha256": "527294054ccd7aab8f1cb220346730317e1d24ce4a314e5955f2e2c3acb427cb",
    "text": "When denominators match, the pieces have the same size. Three quarters is greater than two quarters because three pieces are more than two.",
    "chapter": "Same denominator",
    "equation": [
      [
        3,
        4
      ],
      ">",
      [
        2,
        4
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
        "n": 3,
        "d": 4,
        "label": "Three quarters",
        "colour": "teal"
      },
      {
        "n": 2,
        "d": 4,
        "label": "Two quarters",
        "colour": "gold"
      }
    ],
    "note": "Compare the numerators when denominators match.",
    "line": null,
    "area": null,
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 5,
    "start": 30.636371882086166,
    "end": 36.128843537414966,
    "samples": 121109,
    "audio_sha256": "f22a8aaafc90d2384c7c5616981c1c7ead182041c74d71d8616551019743403f",
    "text": "Now compare one third and one sixth. These wholes are the same length, but the sixths are smaller pieces.",
    "chapter": "One piece: compare its size",
    "equation": [
      [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "?",
      [
        1,
        6
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
        "n": 1,
        "d": 3,
        "label": "One third",
        "colour": "teal"
      },
      {
        "n": 1,
        "d": 6,
        "label": "One sixth",
        "colour": "gold"
      }
    ],
    "note": "More equal pieces in a whole means smaller pieces.",
    "line": null,
    "area": null,
    "context": null
  },
  {
    "index": 6,
    "start": 36.128843537414966,
    "end": 41.525124716553286,
    "samples": 118988,
    "audio_sha256": "f82db040566253501c51edb40b0efccad8939dba22cfc9f03bfbac0b2694b924",
    "text": "So one third is greater than one sixth. A bigger denominator does not always mean a bigger fraction.",
    "chapter": "Unit fractions",
    "equation": [
      [
        1,
        3
      ],
      ">",
      [
        1,
        6
      ]
    ],
    "rows": [
      {
